<title>HONG KONG: Korea First Bank FRN free to trade.</title>
<headline>Korea First Bank FRN free to trade.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Korea First Bank's US$100 million floating rate note issue is now free to trade, arranger Chase Manhattan Asia said Wednesday.</p>
<p>The facility has a final maturity of three years. The issue was priced at par to float at 35 basis points over the six-month London Interbank Offered Rate.</p>
<p>With fees, the all-in return for top-tier managers is 43.5 basis points.</p>
<p>Chase Manhattan Asia is the sole arranger.</p>
<p>--Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2847 4039</p>
